os/arii/tech-dancer/issues/comments/4931002815", "html_url": "https://github.com/arii/tech-dancer/pull/3485#issuecomment-4931002815", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/arii/tech-dancer/issues/3485", "id": 4931002815, "node_id": "IC_kwDOSD1fmM8AAAABJekhvw", "user": {"login": "arii", "id": 342438, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjM0MjQzOA==", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/342438?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii", "html_url": "https://github.com/arii", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-07-10T01:03:25Z", "updated_at": "2026-07-10T01:03:25Z", "body": "### \ud83e\udd16 AI Technical Audit\n\n## ANTI-AI-SLOP\n\nThe refactor significantly improves portability by decoupling from hardcoded paths and utilizing `importlib.resources`. The transition to `.boomtick/logs` in the working directory resolves the issue of write-permissions in site-packages/source trees, which is a critical fix for distributable packages. The code changes are clean, focused, and well-justified.\n\n## FINAL RECOMMENDATION\nApproved with Minor Changes\n\n## DEFINITION of DONE\n1. Update the `agent:prime` script in `package.json`: The script currently calls `python3 boomtick-pkg/cli/dev_tools/resources/build-repo-context.py`. Since this is now part of an installed package, the script should be updated to invoke the installed CLI command (e.g., `td-cli`) or use a proper module entry point if available, rather than assuming a specific source file path, which will break in production environments.\n2. Verify CLI Installation: Confirm that after `pip install .` (or equivalent), the `td-cli` entry point correctly resolves resources regardless of CWD. Run a test from an external directory to ensure imports hold.\n3. Verify tests: Run all tests to ensure the fallback logic in `config.py` and `orchestrator.py` does not mask silent failures in the primary `importlib` logic.\n\n*Review automatically published via RepoAuditor.*", "author_association": "OWNER", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/arii/tech-dancer/issues/comments/4931002815/reactions", "total_count": 1, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 1}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/arii/tech-dancer/issues/comments/4931470304", "html_url": "https://github.com/arii/tech-dancer/pull/3485#issuecomment-4931470304", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/arii/tech-dancer/issues/3485", "id": 4931470304, "node_id": "IC_kwDOSD1fmM8AAAABJfBD4A", "user": {"login": "arii", "id": 342438, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjM0MjQzOA==", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/342438?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii", "html_url": "https://github.com/arii", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/arii/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-07-10T02:39:10Z", "updated_at": "2026-07-10T02:39:10Z", "body": "### \ud83e\udd16 AI Technical Audit\n\n## ANTI-AI-SLOP\n\nThe architectural shift towards standard packaging (distributable Python package + Node MCP server) is a massive improvement for maintainability. The use of `importlib.resources` correctly solves the 'Where are my assets?' problem during runtime. \n\nHowever, there is a persistent 'silent' failure mode regarding the MCP tests. While the PR notes that `github.create_issue.test.ts` fails due to a missing `contract.ts`, leaving broken tests in the repository is a dangerous anti-pattern. Even if the failure is unrelated to the current diff, it erodes trust in the CI suite and makes it harder to diagnose future regressions. \n\nAdditionally, the reliance on absolute paths or assuming `td-cli` exists globally needs to be handled robustly in the MCP config. Ensure the documentation explicitly lists the required `PATH` setup, otherwise, your users will open tickets immediately.\n\n## FINAL RECOMMENDATION\n\nApproved with Minor Changes\n\n## DEFINITION OF DONE\n\n1. Resolve the `contract.ts` missing file error in `boomtick-mcp`. If it's a generated file, ensure it is included in the build/pre-test hook. If it's static, include it.\n2. Fix the failing `github.create_issue.test.ts` test case.\n3. Verify tests, run audit for anti-patterns, and update snapshots if necessary.\n\n*Review automatically published via RepoAuditor.*", "author_association": "OWNER", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/arii/tech-dancer/issues/comments/4931470304/reactions", "total_count": 1, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 1}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}], "created_at": 1783651346.3355665, "expires_at": 1783651646.3355675}